WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.308
When Peter went down into Dorfli that evening, he saw a knot of people a little way off the path.

2
00:00:07.309 --> 00:00:11.033
He wriggled through the crowd to see what they were looking at.

3
00:00:11.034 --> 00:00:15.043
"I saw it when they came through town," said the pastor.

4
00:00:15.044 --> 00:00:18.389
"It must have cost a lot of money."

5
00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:22.916
"I wonder how it was broken," a woman said.

6
00:00:22.917 --> 00:00:28.566
"I don't know," remarked the baker, "but someone will suffer for it.

7
00:00:28.567 --> 00:00:33.300
The gentleman in Frankfurt will want the matter investigated."

8
00:00:33.301 --> 00:00:36.020
It was the ruined wheelchair!

9
00:00:36.021 --> 00:00:44.688
The baker's words frightened Peter and he hurried home, afraid that a policeman might arrive from Frankfurt any moment.

10
00:00:44.689 --> 00:00:52.051
The days that followed were the most joyous days Heidi and Clara spent on the mountain.

11
00:00:52.052 --> 00:00:58.615
Clara awoke each morning with a happy voice inside her that said, "I am well!

12
00:00:58.616 --> 00:01:02.491
I can walk by myself, like other people!"

13
00:01:02.492 --> 00:01:08.581
Every day, she practiced walking with Grandfather, and every day, it got easier.

14
00:01:08.582 --> 00:01:17.199
The exercise gave her quite an appetite, so Grandfather started cutting her bread and cheese in thicker slices.

15
00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:25.013
He also brought out a large jug of foaming milk at every meal and filled her bowl over and over.

16
00:01:25.014 --> 00:01:29.772
During the week, Heidi noticed that Peter was acting strangely.

17
00:01:29.773 --> 00:01:41.248
He never asked if she was coming up the mountain in the morning, but ran off with the goats as soon as Grandfather let Daisy and Dusky out of their pen.

18
00:01:41.249 --> 00:01:46.136
When Heidi asked Grandfather about Peter's behavior, he replied,

19
00:01:46.137 --> 00:01:50.662
"Perhaps Peter fears punishment for something he has done."

20
00:01:50.663 --> 00:01:55.386
Heidi and Clara had planned to give Grandmamma a big surprise.

21
00:01:55.387 --> 00:02:03.895
When she arrived on her horse the next afternoon, she saw Heidi and Clara sitting on the grass under the fir trees.

22
00:02:03.896 --> 00:02:06.838
She quickly climbed down from her horse.

23
00:02:06.839 --> 00:02:12.405
"Why aren't you resting in your chair, Clara?" she asked, worried.

24
00:02:12.406 --> 00:02:15.177
As she got closer, she said,

25
00:02:15.178 --> 00:02:17.099
"Is it really you?

26
00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:21.000
Your cheeks are so round and rosy!

27
00:02:21.001 --> 00:02:23.879
I hardly recognize you!"

28
00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:34.397
It was then that Clara and Heidi stood up and walked over to her, as if it were the most normal thing in the world.

29
00:02:34.398 --> 00:02:37.841
Grandmamma could hardly believe her eyes.

30
00:02:37.842 --> 00:02:42.992
Laughing and crying, she embraced them both over and over again.

31
00:02:42.993 --> 00:02:48.424
She caught sight of Grandfather looking on and smiling.

32
00:02:48.425 --> 00:02:51.576
"My dear Grandfather!

33
00:02:51.577 --> 00:02:56.575
I do believe this is all your doing!" said Grandmamma.

34
00:02:56.576 --> 00:03:00.466
"How much we have to thank you for!"

35
00:03:00.467 --> 00:03:06.579
"You can thank God's good sunshine and mountain air!" said Grandfather, smiling.

36
00:03:06.580 --> 00:03:11.636
"Yes, and don't forget the beautiful milk," said Clara.

37
00:03:11.637 --> 00:03:17.313
"You wouldn't believe how much I have been drinking and how good it is!"

38
00:03:17.314 --> 00:03:20.658
"I can see by your cheeks, Clara.

39
00:03:20.659 --> 00:03:24.306
But we must really telegraph your father.

40
00:03:24.307 --> 00:03:29.035
He must come see you at once!" exclaimed Grandmamma.

41
00:03:29.036 --> 00:03:38.090
So when Peter arrived with the goats a short time later, Grandmamma gave him a note to take to the telegraph office in Dorfli.

42
00:03:38.091 --> 00:03:44.357
Meanwhile, Clara's father, Herr Sesemann, had prepared a little surprise of his own.

43
00:03:44.358 --> 00:03:51.160
He had changed his schedule and, at that very moment, was walking up the mountainside.

44
00:03:51.161 --> 00:03:58.424
He paused, hot and tired from the walk, and saw Peter running down the path with the note in his hand.

45
00:03:58.425 --> 00:04:00.536
"You lad! Come here,"

46
00:04:00.537 --> 00:04:05.669
he cried, meaning to ask if he was on the right path to Grandfather's hut.

47
00:04:05.670 --> 00:04:08.880
"The policeman!" thought Peter.

48
00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:15.015
He let out a frightened cry, ran off the path, and found a large tree to hide behind.

49
00:04:15.016 --> 00:04:18.649
"Oh my," said Herr Sesemann to himself.

50
00:04:18.650 --> 00:04:20.619
"What a shy boy!"

51
00:04:20.620 --> 00:04:26.762
And turning to face the mountain path, he resumed his climb.

